Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:48:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 17/28] Compose A's verifier and head E2Es with the proof-aware
 gateway

P's gateway (witness-failover ce7c1b73) refuses to offer pinned witnesses without a verifier ("no
unverified witness serving"); A's 0c43e4db verifier E2E and A's 9fdc1418 Base head E2E construct it
without one, so on the combined tree both fail at setup (final-a-p). This is a test-only composition
fix:
  * lease-reader-verifier.e2e: the gateway gets the witness-check helper and a root store; the head
    feed pushes each signed head to the root store before serving it (the runtime's order) and signs
    the block's real parent beacon root, so a commitment's hash matches its contents (the native
    listener checks that; Helios alone did not). Every scenario and assertion is unchanged.
  * helios-base-head.e2e: its source-less gateway only gives Helios an execution URL; it now offers
    no pinned witness methods (as P's own unit tests do), so nothing needs or gets verification.
